{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Cocoa Krispies, Choco Krispis, Choco Krispies, Coco Pops, or Choco Pops is a breakfast cereal produced by Kellogg's, coming both as a boxed cereal and as a snack bar with a 'dried milk' covered bottom, to make the cereal with milk tradition portable.","title":"Cocoa Krispies"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is a cocoa flavored version of Rice Krispies.","title":"Cocoa Krispies"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Containing a substance imitating milk chocolate, the cereal can turn milk "chocolatey."","title":"Cocoa Krispies"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Superman: Tower of Power is a drop tower ride currently located at three Six Flags parks, and a former installment at Kentucky Kingdom.","title":"Superman: Tower of Power"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Kellogg Company (also Kellogg's, Kellogg, and Kellogg's of Battle Creek) is an American multinational food manufacturing company headquartered in Battle Creek, Michigan, United States.","title":"Kellogg's"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Kellogg's produces cereal and convenience foods, including cookies, crackers, toaster pastries, cereal bars, fruit-flavored snacks, frozen waffles, and vegetarian foods.","title":"Kellogg's"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The company's brands include Froot Loops, Apple Jacks, Corn Flakes, Frosted Flakes, Rice Krispies, Special K, Cocoa Krispies, Keebler, Pringles, Pop-Tarts, Kashi, Cheez-It, Eggo, Nutri-Grain, Morningstar Farms, and many more.","title":"Kellogg's"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Kellogg's stated purpose is "Nourishing families so they can flourish and thrive."","title":"Kellogg's"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"1 Wall Street Court in the Financial District of Manhattan, also known as The Beaver Building and The Cocoa Exchange (as the former home of the New York Cocoa Exchange) is a triangular-shaped building reminiscent of the Flatiron Building.","title":"1 Wall Street Court"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The building, designed by Clinton and Russell and completed in 1904, is located at the intersection of Wall Street, Pearl Street, and Beaver Street.","title":"1 Wall Street Court"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The O2 Arena (temporarily the sponsor-neutral "North Greenwich Arena", during the 2012 Summer Olympics and 2012 Summer Paralympics), is a multi-purpose indoor arena located in the centre of The O2 entertainment complex on the Greenwich Peninsula in south-east London.","title":"The O2 Arena"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The arena was built under the former Millennium Dome, a large dome-shaped building built to house an exhibition celebrating the turn of the third millennium; as the dome-shaped structure still stands over the arena, "The Dome" remains a name in common usage for the venue.","title":"The O2 Arena"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The arena, as well as the total O2 complex, is named after its primary sponsor, the telecommunications company O.","title":"The O2 Arena"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Conexus Arts Centre, known from 1970 till 2006 (and still largely known) as the Saskatchewan Centre of the Arts, is a theatre complex located within Wascana Centre in Regina, Saskatchewan, which largely replaces former theatres downtown and Darke Hall on the original campus of Regina College, also in Wascana Centre but north of Wascana Lake.","title":"Conexus Arts Centre"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Naming of the Venue as Conexus Arts Centre was possible through a Partner/Sponsor Agreement with the Conexus Credit Union.","title":"Conexus Arts Centre"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Battle Creek, Michigan, United States and Kentucky Kingdom
